ith diffuse slow spike-waves (otherwise known as &#x0201c;petit mal variant&#x0201d;) or Lennox syndrome</article-title><source>Epilepsia</source><year>1966</year><volume>7</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>139</fpage><lpage>179</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4959714</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11-tcrm-5-271"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ohtahara</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ohtsuka</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Kobayashi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Lennox-Gastaut syndrome: a new vista</article-title><source>Psychiatry and Clin Neurosci</source><year>1995</year><volume>49</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>S179</fpage><lpage>S183</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b12-tcrm-5-271"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Roger</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dravet</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Bureau</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Lennox-Gaustaut syndrome</article-title><source>Cleve-land Clin J Med</source><year>1989</year><volume>56</volume><issue>Suppl Pt 2</issue><fpage>S172</fpage><lpage>S180</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b13-tcrm-5-271"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bauer</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Benke</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Bohr</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Lennox-Gaustaut syndrome in adulthood</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Niedermeyer</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Degen</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><source>The Lennox-Gaustaut Syndrome</source><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Alan R. Liss Inc</publisher-name><year>1988</year><fpage>317</fpage><lpage>328</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b14-tcrm-5-271"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Guerrini</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Dravet</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferrari</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Battaglia</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The evolution of epilepsy in the most common genetic forms with mental retadrdation (Down&#x02019;s syndrome and fragile X syndrome)</article-title><source>Pediatr Med Chir</source><year>1993</year><volume>15</volume><issue>Suppl 1</issue><fpage>19</fpage><lpage>22</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8415189</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b15-tcrm-5-271"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beaumanoir</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Lennox-Gastaut syndrome: a personal study</article-title><source>Electroencephalogr Clin Neurophysiol</source><year>1982</year><issue>35</issue><fpage>85</fpage><lpage>99</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b16-tcrm-5-271"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bearmanoir</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Dravet</surname><given-names>CIeLJLp-</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Lennox-Gastaut syndrome</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Roger</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dureau</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Dravet</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Dreifuss</surname><given-names>FE</given-names></name><name><sur